    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Write down and solve a suitable inequation to find the values of $x$ for which the line $y=2x-4$ is below the parabola $y=x^2-3x+2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2x-4<x^2-3x+2$, with solution $x<2$ or $x>3$.",
      "worked": "The line is below the parabola when\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-4&<x^2-3x+2\\\\x^2-5x+6&>0\\\\(x-2)(x-3)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic has zeroes $2$ and $3$ and opens upwards, so its graph is above the $x$-axis outside these zeroes. Hence $x<2$ or $x>3$. The endpoints are excluded because the inequality is strict.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
